      "description": "Watch Ludogorets vs Hapoel Tel Aviv highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 30, 2026. The stage was set for a high-stakes encounter in the UEFA Europa Conference League on July 30, 2026. Both teams stepped onto the pitch knowing that every tactical decision and individual effort would be crucial in this continental showdown. A Tense Opening and Penalty Drama The match ignited early with a series of physical challenges that saw Chico , Petar Stanic , and Son all enter the referee's book within the first 25 minutes. Amidst the tactical battle, Hapoel Tel Aviv managed to break the deadlock in the 16th minute when Emmanuel Boateng found the back of the net following an assist from Stav Turiel . Ludogorets had a golden opportunity to level the score late in the first half when they were awarded a penalty in the 39th minute. However, Kwadwo Duah failed to convert from the spot, leaving the home side frustrated as they headed into the break trailing by a goal after a flurry of additional yellow cards for both sides. Rapid Turnaround and Boateng's Brace The second half began with immediate fireworks as Ludogorets came out with renewed energy. In the 47th minute, Bernard Tekpetey clinical finish equalized the match after being set up by Petar Stanic . The momentum shifted entirely in favor of the hosts just seven minutes later when Alberto Salido struck to give Ludogorets the lead, thanks to an assist from Ivaylo Chochev . The lead was short-lived, however, as Hapoel Tel Aviv responded almost instantly. In the 58th minute, Emmanuel Boateng showcased his scoring prowess once again, netting his second goal of the game to restore parity at 2-2. A Hard-Fought Conclusion As the clock ticked down, both managers turned to their benches to find a winning edge. Ludogorets introduced Rwan Cruz and Emerson Rodriguez , while the visitors brought on Daniel Dappa and Amit Lemkin to stabilize the midfield. The intensity remained high until the very end, with Anton Nedyalkov and Rwan Cruz receiving late bookings as both teams fought desperately for a late winner. Ultimately, the referee’s final whistle confirmed a pulsating draw, leaving everything to play for in the upcoming fixtures of the competition."
